      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "/.*/"
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "value",
        "orientation": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "fintracker-pg"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "rawSql": "SELECT i.symbol || ' · ' || to_char(ed.earnings_date, 'DD Mon') AS \"Next earnings\" FROM earnings_dates ed JOIN instruments i ON i.id = ed.instrument_id WHERE i.in_watchlist AND ed.earnings_date >= CURRENT_DATE ORDER BY ed.earnings_date, i.symbol LIMIT 1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Watchlist",
      "description": "Every watched instrument at its latest close, in its own currency. Moves compare the latest close with the last close at least that long ago (1D: the previous close; YTD: the last close of last year), the same rule as the weekly email. vs 200-day avg: the latest close against the average of the last 200 closes. Below 52w high and 52w range use the closes of the last year (0% of the range = at the low, 100% = at the high). P/E (latest close in the reporting currency over TTM diluted EPS) and market cap (latest close × diluted shares) follow the Ticker Fundamentals rules, and are blank for non-equities, names without filings, and reports older than about 15 months. Click a symbol to chart it below.",
